  "note": "First election of Portadown Borough Council. The Governor (Earl Granville) granted the Urban Council's petition for a charter of incorporation, announced in the Belfast Gazette of 18 July 1947 (Belfast News-Letter, 19 July 1947, p. 5); the borough council of three aldermen and twelve councillors held its first meeting on 2 October 1947, when R. J. Magowan was elected first Mayor (Belfast News-Letter, 3 October 1947, p. 3). Geo. McGowan, returning officer, received the nominations on Friday 5 September 1947: twelve for the twelve councillorships, and four for the three aldermanships. The twelve councillors, nine official Unionist candidates and three unofficial Unionists, were returned unopposed (\"there will thus be no election for the twelve Councillors\")."
